  "whyItMatters": "A heavier section looks safe, but stiffness attracts force: in an indeterminate structure the stiffer member takes a larger share of the moment, so the demands on the joints and on the neighbouring members change, and the member's own ratios drop -- a model that reports a comfortable ratio for a section that is not the one built.",
